dividual who holds a license issued pursuant to this chapter evidencing such person to be qualified to control and have authority of all technical work performed under the authority of the contractor’s mechanical, electrical or plumbing business and assures quality control and is responsible for compliance with all applicable laws, codes and regulations.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"59f7502f-4d59-5b4d-8239-9e08886a7955"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"5.63.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.63.010","content_hash":"a86599738e925e07d9258a58fd0cec98956eff89068fd480e9deb72a4076290f","heading":null,"ordinal":15,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.63.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.63.010:block:15","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.63.010","text":"“Mechanical trade” means the construction, repair or installation of heating, ventilation and air conditioning systems including, but not limited to, sheet metal, gas fitting, heating and cooling, and solid fuels.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"47369663-24ce-525a-8f01-3be11ecdf715"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"5.63.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.63.010","content_hash":"945d3d2e6cbfc6f9ea0a76c3c7c85e931b3f1f1afa60013f27f73fc9b09ccb99","heading":null,"ordinal":16,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.63.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.63.010:block:16","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.63.010","text":"“Nontrade contractor license” means all contractor licenses except those for the licensed trades.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"acdbbd6d-2c25-50aa-8b9a-08d175076bb2"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"5.63.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.63.010","content_hash":"b98928f7ae3e62c0d0a6ec11bd7e7f4151a042e86b628cd84e93c46abb63e9f5","heading":null,"ordinal":17,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.63.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.63.010:block:17","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.63.010","text":"“Plumbing trade” means the construction, repair or installation of plumbing systems including, but not limited to, lawn irrigation, backflow testing/repair and water softener/conditioner systems.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"e93017c4-9eb4-5917-bf53-df43d8c22ecd"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"5.63.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.63.010","content_hash":"cb5c62f92dac040590c7c1e4871ad87c90407d0314fd37bbe1733c2c8c209772","heading":null,"ordinal":18,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.63.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.63.010:block:18","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.63.010","text":"“Trade board” means that board appointed for each licensed trade for the purpose of reviewing code interpretations taken by the Development Services Division, granting variances from the code, reviewing license applications and license suspensions and revocation.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"4becfe6e-bbeb-5e76-9d47-700e7760787f"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"5.63.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.63.010","content_hash":"69501d9cae30a91d1e6e4de5d7f7909fdf31a55f5653a3ca1c4acc68e7176705","heading":null,"ordinal":19,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.63.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.63.010:block:19","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.63.010","text":"“Trade code” means the current version of the electrical, mechanical, and plumbing codes as adopted by the City Council, as the context of this chapter may require.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"b78efdb1-484d-546d-8d86-df689a22de96"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"5.63.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.63.010","content_hash":"cdcd20d1c9984b54778aeebee9be3872968b01726de0162130775eac9441fa84","heading":null,"ordinal":20,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.63.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.63.010:block:20","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.63.010","text":"“Trade contractor license” shall entitle the holder thereof to contract for and to perform any act as a contractor to construct, remodel, repair, or remove the plumbing, electrical, or mechanical systems or facilities for which the contractor has passed the required examination or has in its employ the appropriate master. (Ord. 19938 § 20, 2-10-15.)","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"1a368c68-1570-58d9-a593-384f21bffac6"},{"attributes":{"legacy_definition_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:5.63.010:def:contractor-license"},"citation":"5.63.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.63.010","content_hash":"ed1caa17e9f7baf36cc1d6da94a0357a23b6c4c1ca9c4e76dac82f5ad1630a73","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.63.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.63.010:definition:0","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.63.010","text":null,"type":"definition","workbench_component_id":"7ff555c1-e6a3-516a-8675-6652ae010d13"},{"attributes":{"legacy_definition_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:5.63.010:def:direct-supervision"},"citation":"5.63.010","cita